# Email generation

Every outbound email must pass validation. Every personalized professor claim needs stored supporting evidence.

Use the Saket outreach template in `prompts/email-generation.md`: greeting, first-year UT Dallas CISTech intro, retrieved research topics, a lab-work detail copied from stored evidence, one resume-grounded experience paragraph, a connection paragraph, attached-resume plus spring availability, and `Sincerely, Saket`.

Personalization must change the opening research sentences and the connection paragraph for this professor. Do not only swap the professor name. Do not reuse Huseyin Cavusoglu's economics-of-technology wording unless that claim is in this professor's retrieved evidence.

Writing style: short active sentences, no em dashes, no semicolons, no markdown, no hashtags, no asterisks, no URLs, no citations, no relevance scores. Do not claim the student read a paper unless that evidence exists.

Review Mode is the default. Autopilot may send only when every quality gate passes.
